# Review: MarkdownPlugin autocue flows

QA-4 is driven end to end by the autocue flow `write-and-link.mjs`: it creates the document, types the
heading and list, comments on "Links between pages" and links a new page with `@`. Each step waits for
its target and throws when text is missing, so a broken flow fails the run. It is a demo recorder run
by hand against a bundled build, not a CI test, and it does not assert the navtree name or the new
document's arrival in the navtree. QA-5 shares QA-4's fenced block, so `deus review items` does not
list it and it is not judged here.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

## Verdicts

```mdl
verdict QA-4: An autocue flow drives every step, but it is a hand-run recorder with weak checks.
  status: partial
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-markdown/autocue/write-and-link.mjs]
  note: |
    `write-and-link.mjs` performs all four steps and waits for the editor, comment reply box and
    planks, but it does not check that the navtree takes the heading as the name or that the linked
    document joins the navtree, and nothing runs it in CI.
```
